#: ../../topics/diagrams.rst:101
msgid "A ``graphviz`` file argument reads a DOT file instead of an inline body. ``graph`` and ``digraph`` take the graph name as their argument and wrap the body's edges in the corresponding DOT graph. ``:layout:`` (or Sphinx's ``:graphviz_dot:`` alias) selects the Graphviz layout engine: ``dot`` (default), ``neato``, ``fdp``, ``sfdp``, ``circo``, ``twopi``, ``osage`` or ``patchwork``. A plain ``dot`` or ``graphviz`` Markdown fence also draws a graph; we use the directive form when we need options."
msgstr ""

