msgid "Fletcher builds node-and-arrow diagrams on CeTZ. Its explicit coordinates are useful when position carries meaning."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/diagrams.rst:175
msgid "Share source and refer to figures"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/diagrams.rst:178
msgid "Both directives accept ``:caption:``, ``:alt:``, ``:name:``, ``:class:`` and ``:align:``. We enable ``numfig = true`` in ``conf.toml`` and refer to a named captioned drawing with ``:numref:`` in RST or ``{numref}`` in MyST. For example, :numref:`chapter-typst-circle` is a numbered figure in this book. Alternative text explains the information conveyed by the drawing. It is especially useful for Typst SVGs, which draw letters as outlines."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/diagrams.rst:184
msgid "For a larger drawing we keep Typst source in a file. Guidedog compiles it during the ordinary build."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/diagrams.rst:193
msgid "An inline diagram's imports resolve beside the document containing it. A file diagram's imports resolve beside its Typst file. We can therefore share a local helper library for colors, nodes and sequence diagrams. Changing an imported helper or data file redraws the affected HTML pages. Identical generated images keep their timestamps so unchanged PDF books remain cached."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/diagrams.rst:199
msgid "Packages, limits and failures"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/diagrams.rst:202
msgid "The ``pdf_packages``, ``pdf_fonts`` and ``pdf_font_paths`` settings govern Typst diagrams in both outputs. With ``pdf_packages = \"offline\"``, the compiler uses only packages already installed in Typst's package directories. The default downloads missing packages. After installing a previously missing package or editing fonts, we run a fresh ``guidedog build html -a`` command. Project imports stay below the source directory, including through symlinks. Diagrams must produce one finite page; PNG export is limited to 16 million pixels and 16,384 pixels on either side."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/diagrams.rst:209
msgid "A failed drawing remains visible as source with a warning (``build.graphviz`` or ``build.typst-diagram``; missing or duplicate directive sources report ``sphinx.graphviz.source`` or ``sphinx.typst.source``). We build with ``-W`` when a missing diagram must prevent publication. ``--untrusted`` still compiles Typst diagrams with the embedded compiler, which reads only the source folder and downloads no package, and refuses the files a Graphviz graph names. Text builds show source without compiling a drawing. The :doc:`../howto/typst-diagrams` guide lists every option, source limit and migration step for existing figure files."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/diagrams.rst:215
msgid "Light, dark and print"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/diagrams.rst:218
msgid "Typst diagrams keep their authored colors and receive the same light panel as ordinary Graphviz images in the default dark theme. The adaptive Graphviz palette does not recolor Typst drawings."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/diagrams.rst:220
msgid "A transparent canvas does not change a graph's ink. Dark text can disappear on a dark page. Ordinary graphs therefore keep their chosen colors and receive a light panel in the default dark theme."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/diagrams.rst:224
msgid "For the manual's adaptive palette, add ``:class: graphviz-adaptive`` to the directive. Guidedog adds a fixed stylesheet inside the SVG image. Its dark media query follows the embedding page's ``color-scheme``, including the theme control's explicit selection. No script, external stylesheet or inline page SVG is needed."
msgstr ""

