#: ../../topics/music.rst:12
msgid "We write pitches and durations inside braces. In ``\\relative c'``, each pitch takes the nearest diatonic position to the preceding pitch, then applies its apostrophes or commas. The first pitch uses the reference ``c'``, which is middle C. A number gives the duration's denominator; ``4`` is a quarter note and ``8`` is an eighth note. An omitted duration repeats the preceding duration. A vertical bar checks the measure boundary."
msgstr ""

