#: ../../topics/music.rst:66
msgid "We use four bars of the Joy theme from Beethoven's Symphony No. 9, Op. 125, finale, bars 92-95. We transpose the melody from D major to C major and place it in the treble register, keeping its rhythm and omitting the orchestration, slurs and dynamics. The `CCARH/MuseData score, printed page 8 <https://williamwieland.com/piano/reading/Beethoven/OdetoJoy.pdf>`_, shows the instrumental opening with half notes; some familiar vocal versions divide them into repeated quarter notes."
