#: ../../topics/music.rst:94
msgid "In ``\\fixed c'``, ``c`` is middle C and ``e`` is the E above it. The letters name pitches; ``\\key c \\major`` selects a key with no sharps or flats."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/music.rst:97
msgid "In ``\\time 4/4``, each bar holds four quarter-note beats. As in LilyPond, 4/4 prints as the symbol C, for common time, and 2/2 as a C with a stroke, for cut time; ``\\numericTimeSignature`` prints them as numbers, and ``\\defaultTimeSignature`` brings the symbols back. The first bar has ``e2`` for two beats, then ``f4`` and ``g`` for one beat each; ``g`` inherits the preceding duration. In the last bar, ``e4.`` lasts one and a half beats, ``d8`` half a beat, and ``d2`` two beats. The final D leaves the phrase open because this is an excerpt."
msgstr ""

