#: ../../topics/music.rst:122
msgid "The default pitch language is Nederlands: ``cis`` is C sharp and ``des`` is D flat. We select English names with ``\\language \"english\"`` or ``\\include \"english.ly\"``; examples include ``cs`` and ``df``. Deutsch adds ``h`` for B natural and ``b`` for B flat. These three language includes are built in and read no file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/music.rst:127
msgid "Apostrophes raise octaves and commas lower them. ``\\fixed c' { ... }`` fixes the reference octave instead of following preceding pitches. ``\\transpose c ees { ... }`` transposes spelled pitches and key signatures. Accidentals belong to the pitch name; a key signature does not change a written natural pitch into a sharp pitch. An exclamation mark forces an accidental, and a question mark requests a cautionary accidental. We put these marks after the pitch and before its duration: ``cis'!4`` and ``c'?4``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/music.rst:134
msgid "Durations range from ``1`` through ``128``, with ``\\breve`` for a double whole note. Dots lengthen a duration, and ``*2/3`` scales its exact value. ``r`` is a rest, ``s`` is an invisible spacer, and ``R1*4`` requests four measures of rest in common time. Angle brackets make chords: ``<c' e' g'>4``. ``q`` repeats the preceding chord. A tilde ties equal pitches; parentheses make slurs, and ``\\(`` with ``\\)`` makes a phrasing slur."
msgstr ""

