#: ../../topics/music.rst:244
msgid "Combine staves and lyrics"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/music.rst:247
msgid "We use simultaneous contexts for a score with several staves. Staves and staff groups accept ``instrumentName`` and ``shortInstrumentName`` in a ``\\with`` block, and staves also accept ``\\set Staff.instrumentName`` and ``\\set Staff.shortInstrumentName``. We separate up to four voices on one staff with ``\\\\`` inside ``<< ... >>``. Voices one and three have upward stems; voices two and four have downward stems. ``\\voiceOne``, ``\\voiceTwo``, ``\\voiceThree`` and ``\\voiceFour`` select those policies explicitly, and ``\\oneVoice`` restores automatic single-voice directions. An inner voice beside another voice with the same stem direction stands at least half a notehead aside, and further when needed. Equal rests share a glyph only where no other voice sounds. ``\\shiftOn``, ``\\shiftOnn`` and ``\\shiftOnnn`` move a voice's note columns one, two or three levels aside, and ``\\shiftOff`` sets the level to zero; a voice command restores its own level. Among voices with one stem direction, each lower level puts a column another half notehead aside: right for upward stems, left for downward ones. Dynamics stay below the staff by default in every voice, as in LilyPond (unless ``\\dynamicUp`` or ``^`` places them above); when two voices place signs on the same side at one moment, the later one stacks further out. At most four voices may sound at once on a staff; a fifth is refused. Lyrics attach to a named voice, and separate ``\\lyricsto`` expressions make separate verses."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/music.rst:260
msgid "We can override stems with ``\\stemUp``, ``\\stemDown`` and ``\\stemNeutral`` without changing the voice's column policy."
msgstr ""

